team-1    | self-review: 6 critique items, revised tests/test_bst.py
team-1    |     edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_t3_search_between_values_false: The test uses 4.5 as a between-values probe, but no float-typed key is ever inserted; the comparison relies on mixed int/float ordering which is valid, but the test never checks that search with a float that is equal to an inserted int (e.g. 5.0) returns True, so cross-type equality on search is untested.
team-1    |     edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_t3_search_returns_exact_bool_type: Type check only covers int keys on non-empty and empty trees. Search on a tree whose matching node is reached after several levels and on a missing value after the descent exits via None are both exercised only with ints; the bool return on the NaN and incomparable-type error paths is not asserted.
team-1    |     edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_t3_search_after_duplicate_inserts_still_true: Duplicate-insert coverage for search only uses the original values; it does not check that search still works after a duplicate of a non-root value on a deeper tree where the duplicate insert descends past nodes, nor that the node count is unchanged afterwards.
team-1    |     edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_t3_search_root_left_right_leaf: Leaf coverage uses only the leaves 1 and 9 on a tree of depth 2; the deeper-level leaves (a left child of a left child, right child of a right child) are not explicitly exercised, so a bug that only fails at depth 3 in search's left-branch or right-branch loop would pass.
team-1    |     edge_case bst.py:search (iterative loop): Search must not mutate the tree or recurse; a regression that inserts on search or caches state would go unnoticed. Also, repeated search calls on the same tree are not verified as idempotent.
team-1    |     edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_t3_search_below_min_false / above_max: Below-min and above-max probes use only the global min and max of one specific tree. A bug where search compares only against the root (e.g. returning True when the value is at the boundary of a subtree) would not be caught by values just outside the extremes such as min-1 and max+1 with a single-element tree.
