team-1    | self-review: 8 critique items, revised tests/test_bst.py
team-1    |     bug tests/test_bst.py:_build / test_t5_build_and_query_under_lowered_recursion_limit: Lowering sys.setrecursionlimit to current depth+60 is fragile: pytest's own frames and the assertion-rewrite machinery may already be near the limit, so the test can fail with RecursionError from pytest or from the test harness rather than from the BST, and results vary across pytest versions and plugins. Also, CPython 3.12+ may raise differently when the limit is set below the current depth.
team-1    |     bug tests/test_bst.py:test_t6_insert_go_left_and_right_at_depth_three / test_t5_*: _max_depth and _count_nodes read private attributes (tree._root, node.left/right). If the implementation names these differently (e.g. _Node fields), these helpers raise AttributeError and many tests fail for reasons unrelated to behaviour. The helpers are not guarded.
team-1    |     bug tests/test_bst.py:test_t4_failed_insert_creates_no_node / test_t4_successful_insert_creates_exactly_one_node: monkeypatch replaces bst_module._Node with a subclass, but the module's insert likely references the global name _Node at call time, which works only if insert looks it up dynamically. _CountingNode also subclasses the original _Node, so if bst.py's _Node has __slots__ or a different constructor signature, super().__init__(value) may break. These tests depend on implementation details not in the spec.
team-1    |     edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_t2_numeric_equal_values_treated_as_duplicates / test_t4_mixed_int_float_cross_type_duplicates: Inserting True alongside 1 relies on bool/int equality; this couples the test to Python equality semantics and would also pass if the implementation compared by identity-insensitive hashing. Acceptable, but it asserts behaviour the spec does not state (spec only says duplicates are ignored).
team-1    |     edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_t4_signed_zero_is_single_value: Asserts inorder()==[0] after inserting 0, -0.0, 0.0; this passes only if the first-inserted representation is kept. Fine, but test_t4_int_first/float_first already cover representation; the -0.0 test does not check which zero is returned.
team-1    |     edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_t5_ascending_5000_inorder_and_search: Asserts _max_depth == 5000 exactly, which encodes the unbalanced-BST design choice. Any future self-balancing change would break this test even though behaviour is correct.
team-1    |     edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_t4_strings_sorted_by_codepoint / test_t4_empty_string_and_unicode_strings_sorted: Sorting assertions compare against sorted(words), which is fine, but no test covers search/insert of values equal in a str tree with differing case, nor non-ASCII ordering beyond one element; low value gaps only.
team-1    |     edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_t6_public_api_present: Task requires AC1-AC10 each mapped to a test, but the comment mapping cites T1-T5 criteria and the AC IDs are never enumerated in the file; the acceptance mapping cannot be verified against AC1-AC10 as stated in the task, and no test is labelled by AC number.
